---
import AppLayout from '../../../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
import Topbar from '../../../components/Topbar.astro';
import Footer from '../../../components/Footer.astro';
import AppRail from '../../../components/AppRail.astro';
import Chapter from '../../../components/Chapter.astro';
import { getApp } from '../../../data/apps';
const app = getApp('hyttepermen');
---
<AppLayout app={app} title={`Privacy · ${app.name}`}>
  <Topbar variant="app" />
  <div class="app-page">
    <AppRail app={app} current="personvern" />
    <div class="app-flow">
      <Chapter num="01" label="Overview" title={`Privacy, in <em>plain English</em>.`}>
        <p class="lede">{app.name} is an iOS app for shared cabin management. We run no servers of our own. All data is stored locally on your device and synced via your own iCloud account. We have no access to cabin, stay, checklist, chat or photo data.</p>
        <p>We use no tracking, no ads and no analytics. You can delete all your data from the app at any time (the Shed → Settings → Delete all my data).</p>
        <p class="muted">Last updated · 17 May 2026.</p>
      </Chapter>

      <Chapter num="02" label="Data controller" title={`Who's <em>behind it</em>.`}>
        <p>The data controller for personal information is:</p>
        <p><strong>Jonas Haug</strong></p>
        <p>Konvallveien 20</p>
        <p>3047 Drammen, Norway</p>
        <p>Email: <a class="tx-link" href="mailto:jonas@haugogdatter.no">jonas@haugogdatter.no</a></p>
      </Chapter>

      <Chapter num="03" label="Data you enter" title={`What you <em>put in yourself</em>.`}>
        <p>You can enter information into the app. You choose what to add:</p>
        <p>· <strong>Name</strong> and role at the cabin</p>
        <p>· <strong>Cabin information</strong> (name, address, photos)</p>
        <p>· <strong>Checklists</strong> and <strong>shopping lists</strong></p>
        <p>· <strong>Cabin log entries</strong> (including photos and drawings)</p>
        <p>· <strong>Maintenance records</strong> and <strong>meter readings</strong> (water, power, firewood)</p>
        <p>· <strong>Chat messages</strong> on the Hearth and during active trips</p>
        <p>· <strong>Practical info</strong> (Binder cards: wifi, codes, alarm codes, suppliers)</p>
      </Chapter>

      <Chapter num="04" label="Technical data" title={`What the <em>app knows</em>.`}>
        <p>· <strong>Device and OS version</strong> is used only locally for compatibility checks. If you send feedback by email from the app, this information is attached automatically.</p>
        <p>· <strong>iCloud account ID</strong> is used as an identifier for sync. It is handled by Apple, we do not see it.</p>
        <p class="muted">Settings and preferences are stored locally on the device (UserDefaults).</p>
      </Chapter>

      <Chapter num="05" label="What we don't collect" title={`<em>No tracking.</em> No ads.`}>
        <p>{app.name} does not collect:</p>
        <p>· Location data, contacts or calendar contents</p>
        <p>· IDFA, advertising ID or any tracking identifier</p>
        <p>· Crash reports or usage statistics</p>
        <p>We do not use Google Analytics, Firebase, Crashlytics, TelemetryDeck or similar. There are no ads in the app.</p>
      </Chapter>

      <Chapter num="06" label="Where it lives" title={`<em>Locally</em>, iCloud, met.no.`}>
        <p>· <strong>Cabin, stay, checklist, chat, photo and card data</strong> is stored locally on your device and in your private iCloud account via Apple's NSPersistentCloudKitContainer.</p>
        <p>· <strong>Invitation codes for shared cabins</strong> live in CloudKit Public Database (Apple's servers). Only the code itself and cabin affiliation, no personal data.</p>
        <p>· <strong>Settings and preferences</strong> are stored locally on the device (UserDefaults).</p>
        <p>· <strong>Weather data</strong> is fetched from <a class="tx-link" href="https://www.met.no/om-oss/personvern" target="_blank" rel="noopener">met.no</a> when needed. The request contains only the geographic area of the cabin, no user information.</p>
        <p class="muted">Apple Inc. is the processor for iCloud services. Apple's privacy policy applies to that processing: <a class="tx-link" href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">apple.com/legal/privacy</a>.</p>
      </Chapter>

      <Chapter num="07" label="Sharing and AI" title={`CloudKit, <em>Apple and OpenAI</em>.`}>
        <p>When you create a shared cabin and invite family members, cabin data is synced to their iCloud accounts via Apple's CloudKit Sharing. You decide who is invited and what role they have. We do not see who is a member or what is shared.</p>
        <p>Plus features such as smart checklist, area guide auto-fill, AI expense insights and natural-language shopping lists send a short text request to OpenAI's API (gpt-4o-mini) when you actively use the feature. The request contains the context you've entered, not names of people or photos.</p>
        <p class="muted">If you don't use these features, OpenAI is not contacted. AI features can be turned off in settings. See <a class="tx-link" href="https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenAI's privacy policy</a> (gpt-4o-mini is not used to train their models).</p>
        <p>We do not share personal data with third parties beyond this. We have no agreements with ad networks, analytics providers or data brokers.</p>
      </Chapter>

      <Chapter num="08" label="Purchases" title={`Plus is handled by <em>Apple</em>.`}>
        <p>{app.name} Plus is a one-time purchase of 99 NOK handled entirely by Apple via the App Store and StoreKit. Apple processes payment information. We only receive a signal that the purchase is complete, and do not see card numbers or billing addresses.</p>
      </Chapter>

      <Chapter num="09" label="Legal basis and retention" title={`<em>GDPR</em> Art. 6.`}>
        <p>Processing is based on the following:</p>
        <p>· <strong>Necessary for performance of the service</strong> (GDPR Art. 6(1)(b)) — for the app to function we must store the data you enter.</p>
        <p>· <strong>Legitimate interest</strong> (GDPR Art. 6(1)(f)) — for feedback by email.</p>
        <p>Data is retained for as long as you use the app. When you delete a cabin or entry, it is removed immediately from your device and iCloud. When you delete all data (the Shed → Settings → Delete all my data), all local data, all data in your private iCloud, and all active invitation codes in CloudKit Public Database are removed. Deletion cannot be undone.</p>
      </Chapter>

      <Chapter num="10" label="Your rights" title={`<em>Access</em>, rectification, deletion.`}>
        <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to access, rectification, deletion, data portability, restriction and objection. You can exercise most of these rights directly in the app:</p>
        <p>· <strong>Access and portability:</strong> the Shed → Settings → Export cabin data (creates a JSON file with all your data)</p>
        <p>· <strong>Deletion:</strong> the Shed → Settings → Delete all my data</p>
        <p>· <strong>Rectification:</strong> edit directly in the app</p>
        <p>For other requests, contact <a class="tx-link" href="mailto:jonas@haugogdatter.no">jonas@haugogdatter.no</a>. You also have the right to lodge a complaint with <a class="tx-link" href="https://www.datatilsynet.no" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Datatilsynet</a> (the Norwegian Data Protection Authority) if you believe the processing is unlawful.</p>
      </Chapter>

      <Chapter num="11" label="Security, children and changes" title={`Protection and <em>contact</em>.`}>
        <p>· Data is transferred via Apple's encrypted CloudKit service (TLS/HTTPS).</p>
        <p>· iCloud data is protected by your Apple ID and your device passcode/Face ID.</p>
        <p>· Sensitive fields (wifi passwords, codes, alarm codes) are hidden by default and require a tap to reveal.</p>
        <p>{app.name} is not directed to children under 13. If you as a parent or guardian become aware that a child under 13 has entered data without consent, contact us to have the data deleted.</p>
        <p>We may update this policy when needed. Significant changes are announced in the app. The current version is always available here with a new "Last updated" date.</p>
        <p class="muted">Questions about privacy: <a class="tx-link" href="mailto:jonas@haugogdatter.no">jonas@haugogdatter.no</a>. See also the <a class="tx-link" href="/en/hyttepermen/vilkar/">terms of service</a>.</p>
      </Chapter>
    </div>
  </div>
  <Footer label={`${app.name} · Privacy`} />
</AppLayout>
